  "progress": "Verified 3 candidates so far. (1) fs_enet-main.c: NAPI poll fs_enet_napi (netif_napi_add:1023, scheduled from hardirq fs_enet_interrupt 344/352, request_irq:733) takes plain spin_lock(&fep->tx_lock) at 99; process-context fs_enet_close (.ndo_stop:896) takes same plain lock at 765 inside spin_lock_irqsave(&fep->lock) at 764 (IRQs off, BH NOT); zero spin_lock_bh in file; napi_disable at 761, free_irq at 772 AFTER lock section. REPORTED. (2) altera_tse_main.c: NAPI poll tse_poll (netif_napi_add:1577, scheduled from altera_isr 549/554, request_irq 1219/1228) -> tse_tx_complete takes plain spin_lock(&priv->tx_lock) at 463; process tse_shutdown (.ndo_stop:1320) plain at 1298 under mac_cfg_lock 1297; xmit uses spin_lock_bh at 579 (only _bh site). REPORTED low. (3) cassini.c: cas_poll (NAPI, napi_schedule 2461/2512/2568) -> cas_tx:2592 -> cas_tx_ringN takes plain spin_lock(&cp->tx_lock[ring]) at 1861; hardirq cas_interrupt also calls cas_tx at 2561 under cp->lock irqsave; workqueue cas_reset_task (INIT_WORK:5049, schedule_work from tx_timeout:2720/2723, link:3878/3883, cas_write_phy errors:1828/1832, cas_corrupt_rx_buf?) calls cas_lock_all_save at 4031 = spin_lock_irqsave(&cp->lock)+cas_lock_tx plain spin_lock_nested(tx_lock[i]) at 249; cas_close (.ndo_stop) napi_disable at 4309 then cas_lock_all_save at 4328; free_irq AFTER lock section at 4335. cas_interrupt hardirq calls cas_tx directly at 2561 while cas_reset_task holds tx_lock with only IRQs disabled - hardirq cannot fire on same CPU (IRQs disabled) so that direction is blocked, but cas_poll NAPI (scheduled by hardirq before disable window) vs workqueue holder is the live window. REPORTED medium/low. Next: examine remaining NAPI-driver plain locks (igb, forcedeth, mvneta, cpmac, enic, bcm63xx_enet, ravb, natsemi, via-rhine, tsi108, korina, cxgb3) and tasklet files (usbnet, lan78xx, rt2x00, b43legacy, jme, ath5k, hostap, mwl8k) for process-context plain holders.",
  "candidates": [
    {"path": "drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fs_enet/fs_enet-main.c", "line": 765, "status": "reported", "reason": "NAPI poll fs_enet_napi:99 plain tx_lock vs process close:765 plain tx_lock inside irqsave(&fep->lock); no _bh in file"},
    {"path": "drivers/net/ethernet/altera/altera_tse_main.c", "line": 1298, "status": "reported", "reason": "NAPI tse_poll->tse_tx_complete:463 plain tx_lock vs tse_shutdown:1298 plain; xmit correctly _bh at 579; napi_disable/free_irq narrow window"},
    {"path": "drivers/net/ethernet/sun/cassini.c", "line": 249, "status": "reported-pending-final-check", "reason": "cas_lock_tx plain spin_lock_nested under workqueue cas_reset_task:4031 and cas_close:4328 (IRQs off, BH on) vs NAPI cas_poll->cas_tx:2592->cas_tx_ringN:1861 plain; cas_poll also takes cp->lock irqsave at 2591 so the NAPI side enters with IRQs disabled - need to confirm the NAPI path is not already fully serialized by cp->lock on the holder side (holder takes cp->lock first, so NAPI side spins on cp->lock before reaching tx_lock: that direction is blocked; but the reverse - workqueue holds tx_lock-only sections? all cas_lock_all sites take cp->lock first) - RE-EXAMINE before finalizing"}
  ]
}

